#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:205
#: 1bfc49d76a5b4cbe828c0f99a2f8de86
msgid "Behind the scenes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:208
#: 2cb341970401494a9633528c6af1037a
msgid ""
"``qvm-sync-appmenus`` works by invoking the *GetAppMenus* :doc:`Qubes "
"service </developer/services/qrexec>` in the target domain. This service "
"enumerates applications installed in that qube and sends formatted info back "
"to dom0 which creates ``.desktop`` files in the app qube/template directory "
"of dom0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:210
#: 9680fe8ebd854bdfb552ad30f368da44
msgid ""
"For Linux qubes the service script is in :file:`/etc/qubes-rpc/"
"qubes.GetAppMenus``. In Windows it’s a PowerShell script located in :file:`c:"
"\\Program Files\\Invisible Things Lab\\Qubes OS Windows Tools\\qubes-rpc-"
"services\\get-appmenus.ps1` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:212
#: 2fda41370c724acfb20d2821b60c6889
msgid ""
"The list of installed applications for each app qube is stored in "
"dom0’s :file:`~/.local/share/qubes-appmenus/{<QUBE_NAME>}/apps.templates`. "
"Each menu entry is a file that follows the `.desktop file format <https://"
"standards.freedesktop.org/desktop-entry-spec/desktop-entry-spec-"
"latest.html>`__ with some wildcards (``%VMNAME%``, ``%VMDIR%``). "
"Applications selected to appear in the menu are stored in :file:`~/.local/"
"share/qubes-appmenus/{<QUBE_NAME>}/apps` and in :file:`~/.local/share/"
"applications/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/app-menu-shortcut-troubleshooting.rst:214
#: afc72e4dd7104415bbdc4a80b08d2d2c
msgid ""
"The whitelist given to ``qvm-appmenu --set-whitelist`` is stored as a "
"feature called ``menu-items``, where each desktop entry is separated by a "
"space."
msgstr ""

